--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Asterisk (GPLv2) posture
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Asterisk is licensed under GPLv2 (with the OpenSSL linking exception). OpenPhonex
does NOT fork, bundle, modify, statically or dynamically link, or redistribute
Asterisk or any Asterisk binary. The provided `Dockerfile.asterisk` installs
Asterisk from the operator's own distribution package repository at the
operator's build/run time, so the operator obtains Asterisk directly from
upstream under GPLv2. OpenPhonex distributes zero GPL-licensed code.

OpenPhonex's two contributions are arms-length and independently licensed under
Apache-2.0:

  (a) the Asterisk `.conf` / `.conf.template` files in `configs/asterisk/` are
      configuration data (an interface), authored by OpenPhonex; and
  (b) the Python gateway communicates with Asterisk only over the ARI
      HTTP/WebSocket network API — a network boundary, not linking and not a
      derivative work.

Therefore no GPL copyleft obligation reaches OpenPhonex code, and Apache-2.0 is
compatible with this deployment model.

